The decision engine in backend/ is a C port of the XKEYSCORE portion of
Intel Phi Jev (https://github.com/Lasimeri/Intel-Phi-Jev): ARTICHOKE, the
prompt layouts, the judge and the /v1/systemone server. Intel Phi Jev began
as an import of jev-rs by Yijun Yu and contributors
(https://github.com/yijunyu/jev-rs), used under the MIT license or the
Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE); that notice is kept here
for the portions that descend from it.

The confidence formulas follow TypeSafe AI's system-one-adapter (MIT
License, Copyright (c) 2026 TypeSafe AI).

The JSON reader and writer (backend/src/json.c) reproduce the behaviour of
serde_json 1.0.151 and zmij 1.0.23 (MIT OR Apache-2.0, David Tolnay and
contributors); no code is copied from them.

